    "context.network": "Two communication stages: client → preview application → HTTP request from the application to the fetch destination. The requesting user’s source differs from the destination the application attempts to contact. Treat each redirect target as another possible connection.",
    "context.normalBehavior.0": "Normally, the service retrieves information from permitted external pages and returns a preview.",
    "context.normalBehavior.1": "Some requests are rejected by URL or redirect-target validation. Rejection and an actual connection are different outcomes.",
    "context.normalBehavior.2": "The user-facing HTTP response and the result of the server-side fetch are different records.",
    "context.logSources.0.description": "HTTP requests and responses. Check the source, requested URL, status, response size, and request_id.",
    "context.logSources.1.description": "Text audit records of application decisions and business events. Correlate them with HTTP results.",
